dialogue trust_barbarian_1
title: Red hands
trigger: Trust barbarian level=1
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Barbarian sits apart from the fire, winding a strip of white cloth around split knuckles, pulling each turn tight with their teeth.
  * That's a Choir banner you're bleeding on. -> banner
    do: AddTrust $with 2
  * You were first in and last out today. I saw. -> first
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * You took the first watch at the ford, that first night. Have you slept properly since? -> watch
    if: FlagSet founding:watch_barbarian
    do: AddTrust $with 4

node banner hero
  Off the tithe wagon. The white wraps well, and I like knowing whose cloth I bleed on. Seems fair to make it work for us for once.
  -> rage

node first hero
  First in, aye. Last out because I didn't know it was over. That's the bit you didn't see.
  -> rage

node watch hero
  Sleep's for people who don't hear wheels in the dark. I'll catch up on it when the Captain stops chasing us.
  -> rage

node rage hero
  Near the end today, I lost the count. For a breath I couldn't tell the slime from the Cleric. It comes on me like that when the blood's up. The red, we called it at home.
  -> home

node home hero
  The old ones back there said the red would get me killed or get someone else killed, and they didn't much mind which. So. Now you know what's walking behind your wagon.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Barbarian watches the Commander's face, waiting for the flinch.
  * That anger is half the reason we're still alive. I'd rather have it than not. -> trusted
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag barbarian:rage_trusted
  * Then we find a word that brings you back. You pick it, and I'll shout it. -> word
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag barbarian:rage_word
  * If it ever turns on the party, you sit the next fight out. -> leash
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag barbarian:rage_leashed

node trusted hero
  Nobody's ever said that and meant it. Careful, Commander. I'll hold you to it the day I get it wrong.
  -> origin

node word hero
  A word. Huh. Then shout "Saltmoss". That's where the red started. It'll remind me who it's for.
  -> origin

node leash hero
  Hard, but fair. I'd say the same if it were anyone else swinging that close to the Cleric. I'll not like it, mind.
  -> origin

node origin hero
  It started on a tithe day. Not this last one. Another, years back. I'll tell you about it some night, when I know you better than I do.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Barbarian ties off the last turn of white cloth, flexes the hand once, and goes to take a place by the fire.
